workedExamples.question_text:
(a) A rectangle measures $1.7\text{ m}$ by $93\text{ cm}$. Find its perimeter in centimetres.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (3.4,1.86);
\path (1.7,0) node[below] {$1.7\text{ m}$} (3.4,0.93) node[right] {$93\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
(b) A square has side length $340\text{ mm}$. Find its perimeter in centimetres.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (2,2);
\path (1,0) node[below] {$340\text{ mm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

(a) A triangle has perimeter $5.8\text{ m}$ and known sides $2.15\text{ m}$ and $170\text{ cm}$. Find the third side in centimetres.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (3.9,0);
\coordinate (C) at (2.838,3.230);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--cycle;
\path (1.95,0) node[below] {?} (2.838,3.230) node[above] {};
\path (A)--(C) node[midway,above left] {$2.15\text{ m}$};
\path (B)--(C) node[midway,right] {$170\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
(b) A rectangle has perimeter $0.86\text{ km}$ and length $247\text{ m}$. Find its width in metres.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (3.705,2.745);
\path (1.8525,0) node[below] {$247\text{ m}$} (3.705,1.3725) node[right] {?};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Find the perimeter of this five-sided garden in centimetres. The diagram is not to scale.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (3,0);
\coordinate (C) at (3.8,1.8);
\coordinate (D) at (2,3);
\coordinate (E) at (0,2);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--(D)--(E)--cycle;
\path (A)--(B) node[midway,below] {$1.4\text{ m}$};
\path (B)--(C) node[midway,right] {$90\text{ cm}$};
\path (C)--(D) node[midway,above right] {$1.1\text{ m}$};
\path (D)--(E) node[midway,above left] {$800\text{ mm}$};
\path (E)--(A) node[midway,left] {$95\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A rectangle is $5.6\text{ cm}$ wide. Its length is $3.2\text{ cm}$ longer than its width. Find its perimeter.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (3.52,2.24);
\path (1.76,0) node[below] {length} (3.52,1.12) node[right] {$5.6\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.solution_text:
Find the length first. Both measurements are in centimetres.

$\begin{aligned}\text{Length}&=5.6+3.2\\&=8.8\text{ cm}\end{aligned}$

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (3.52,2.24);
\path (1.76,0) node[below] {$8.8\text{ cm}$} (3.52,1.12) node[right] {$5.6\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Count both pairs of sides.

$\begin{aligned}P&=2\times(8.8+5.6)\\&=2\times14.4\\&=28.8\text{ cm}\end{aligned}$

